/**
 * C1: BUYING A HOME (docs/43-lessons.md §15.3, part 3).
 *
 * Winter, and the family buys a home. The morning show on what a home costs
 * and Urmas putting the rent up, a viewing with Raivo, the seller's agent, the
 * bank's loan offer from Anneli, the survey that finds damp in the cellar, and
 * the figures Anna writes up for Helgi's residents' newsletter; then the price,
 * negotiated with Raivo when another buyer appears. One pattern is explained
 * here and nowhere else in the level: the formal links built from verbs that an
 * offer and a contract run on ({võrreldes}, {vastavalt}, {arvestades},
 * {hoolimata}, {vaatamata}, {selmet}), with having a thing done ({lasta teha})
 * (`connective`, lesson 13, worked out lesson by lesson after it). B2's
 * nominalization is taken into the prose of a loan offer, and every lesson reads
 * a real text and is asked about it, its statements matched to its sections.
 * The part writes the paper's neutral summary of figures, and ends on a
 * negotiation where the move is pushing back on a number and holding your price
 * (§15.5).
 *
 * Who is who is `docs/reviews/c1-cast.md`. Three strangers are new names used
 * in one lesson only: Riho, another viewer at the flat (lesson 14), Kerli, the
 * guest on the morning show who explains a home loan (lesson 15), and Aivar,
 * the surveyor (lesson 16).
 *
 * In preview (`preview.ts`) until C1 is the course, and held to every check a
 * lesson is (`npx tsx scripts/check-lesson-part.ts --part c1-kodu`).
 */

